{% doc %}
  The ONE place that decides which cart drawer this visitor gets — the
  switch of the cart-drawer A/B test (A/B app: SPEC-component-experiments).

  The A/B app writes the hidden cart attribute `_tl_abc_cart_drawer` = "B" for
  visitors in arm B and clears it otherwise; Shopify renders every page per
  cart, so Liquid sees it on every page and on every `cart?view=mini`
  re-render. Absent or anything but "B" → arm A (the current drawer), so the
  theme behaves exactly as before whenever no test is running.

  To ship B permanently: change the condition to `!= 'A'`.

  @param {string} part - shell (drawer + scripts, from Header) | content (cart?view=mini)
  @param {product[]} [up_selling] - Header's up-selling products (arm A shell only)

  @example
  {% render 'cart-drawer-arm', part: 'shell', up_selling: section.settings.up_selling_products %}
{% enddoc -%}
{%- if part != 'content' -%}
  {%- comment -%}Drawer analytics for BOTH arms (claudedocs/gtm/CART-DRAWER-TRACKING.md).{%- endcomment -%}
  <script src="{{ 'cart-analytics.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{%- endif -%}
{%- if cart.attributes['_tl_abc_cart_drawer'] == 'B' -%}
  {%- if part == 'content' -%}
    {%- render 'CartDrawerV3Content' -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- render 'CartDrawer' -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- if part == 'content' -%}
    {%- render 'CartDrawerContent' -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- render 'MiniCart', up_selling: up_selling -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
